# Build-context exclusions. Two jobs: keep secrets out of the image (GC2 — no secret in git, and
# none in an artefact either), and keep the context small enough that a rebuild is cheap.

# Secrets first and unconditionally. apps/core/.env is gitignored and lives on the build host.
# This also covers docker/prod/.env.prod.example, which nothing in any image needs.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Host artefacts. node_modules is reinstalled from the frozen lockfile inside the image; dist is
# recompiled inside the image, and copying a stale one in would be rule 5's hazard by another
# route.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Repository furniture that no stage reads.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.superpowers
.nvmrc
docs
LICENSE
README.md

**/*.log
**/.DS_Store

# NOT excluded, deliberately: `docker/`. A .dockerignore governs the CONTEXT, not the Dockerfile,
# so it applies to every build rooted at this directory — including `docker build -f
# docker/prod/db.Dockerfile .` (D8/FORK-C's Postgres+pgBackRest image, T4). Excluding `docker/`
# here would make that build unable to COPY its own pgbackrest.conf, for a saving of a few KB.
# Nothing in this file's stages copies `docker/`, so it never reaches an image.
